---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const pageTitle = "Rama Krishna's Portfolio";
---

<Layout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
	<div class='gif'>
		<img width='300' height='259' alt='ManWorkingOnLaptop' src='/space.webp' />
	</div>

	<h1>Rama Krishna</h1>
	<span class='badge'>Computer Engineer</span>
	<!-- <span class='badge'>Digital Craftsman</span> -->

	<h2>About</h2>
	<p>Low-level engineer passionate about hardware-accelerated computing.</p>
	<p>
	I work at the hardware-software boundary — programming FPGAs, DPUs, and
    similar platforms to squeeze out performance wherever it's needed most:
    robotics, high-speed networking, LLM inference, and beyond.
	</p>
	<div class='center'>
		<a href='/works/'>
			<button class='btn'>My portfolio</button>
		</a>
	</div>

	<h2>Skills</h2>
	<div class='skills_grid'>
		<h3>Languages</h3>
		<div class='skills center'>
			<p>C</p>
			<p>C++</p>
			<p>Python</p>
			<p>Javascript</p>
			<p>VHDL</p>
		</div>
		<h3>Technologies</h3>
		<div class='skills center'>
			<p>FPGA</p>
			<p>Microcontrollers</p>
			<p>Linux</p>
		</div>
		<h3>Tools</h3>
		<div class='skills center'>
			<p>MATLAB</p>
			<p>Vivado</p>
			<p>Git</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2>Work Experience</h2>
	<div class='education-timeline'>
		<div class='experience'>
			<p>2026 - Present</p>
			<p>Student Research Assistant</p>
			<p>Computer Networks Group, Paderborn University</p>
			<p>Working on accelerating serverless LLM inference</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2>Education</h2>
	<div class='education-timeline'>
		<div class='experience'>
			<p>2025 - Present</p>
			<p>Paderborn University</p>
			<p>Computer Engineering <span class='badge'>M.Sc</span></p>
		</div>
		<div class='experience'>
			<p>2019 - 2023</p>
			<p>National Institute of Technology, Trichy</p>
			<p>Electrical and Electronics Engineering <span class='badge'>B.Tech</span></p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2>Projects</h2>
	<div>
		<h3>Hardware/Software Co-Design of Distributed Robotic Systems</h3>
	</div>
	<div>
		<h3>A Novel Three-Port Converter for Battery and Ultra Capacitor based Electric Vehicle</h3>
		<a href='https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10245382' target='_blank'>IEEE</a>
		<p>
			This research presents a three-port DC-DC converter for connecting a Li-ion battery and an ultracapacitor to the
			drive system of an electric vehicle (EV). The suggested converter handles pulse currents in an EV drive train by
			utilizing an ultracapacitor and steady state current with a battery. The ultracapacitor and DC bus ports can
			transmit power in both directions, allowing the ultracapacitor to supply and absorb peak currents during
			acceleration and braking.
		</p>
	</div>

